One of the long-standing gripes about NetHack is its binary resistance
system. Well, now this Resistance patch is here to improve it. Don't
worry, it isn't going to be any more complex than the speed system.
There's now two levels of resistance - half (intrinsic) and full
(extrinsic).

* Half resistance is intrinsic resistance given by level gain or by
eating stuff.
* Full resistance is everything else (including intrinsics given at
level 1.)

Also, "magic resistance" has been divided into two separate
resistances, outlined below.

DIVISION OF MAGIC AND SPELL RESISTANCE:

* Magic resistance now only protects against magic missiles and magical
explosions.
* Spell resistance now only protects against enemy spells (and, ahem,
death rays - but I might change this in the future).

* Gray dragon scale mail only provides magic resistance.
* The cloak of magic resistance is now the "cloak of spell resistance".
* There is a new amulet: "amulet versus spells".
* There is a new ring: "ring of magic resistance."
* Magicbane now provides both magic resistance and spell resistance -
but only when wielded!
* The Orb of Detection, The Sceptre of Might, The Magic Mirror of
Merlin, The Eyes of the Overworld, The Platinum Yendorian Express Card
and The Eye of the Aethiopica now only provide magic resistance.

CHANGES TO ABILITY GAINS:

Because resistances given at level 1 are full, and resistances given
above level 1 are half, the following changes have had to occur:
* Barbarians now gain half poison resistance at level 3.
* Monks now gain:
	half sleep resistance at level 3
	half poison resistance at level 5
	stealth at level 7
	warning at level 9
	searching at level 11
	half fire resistance at level 13
	half cold resistance at level 14
	half shock resistance at level 15
	teleport control at level 17
* Valkyries now gain half cold resistance at level 3.
* Wizards now gain half magic resistance at level 20.
* Elves now start at level 1 with full sleep resistance.
* Gray dragon corpses now confer half magic resistance when eaten.

BONUS FEATURES:
Element damage has been standardised:
* All fire damage will reduce your max HP by a small percentage of the
damage recieved.
* All non-missile mana damage has a chance (reduced if you have magic
resistance) that you will "absorb the magical energy" and gain energy.

ALSO:
* Half sleep resistance will halve the amount of time that you are
asleep.
* Half disintegration resistance will cause disintegration attacks to
only halve your HP.
* Half poison resistance is sufficient to protect you from deadly
poison.

